# Firmware versions (docs/firmware_versions.md): `version` says them
# machine-readably; an HV board running another firmware than the one this
# LV firmware carries faults the drive (HV_VERSION_ERROR, 19) and it can't
# enable, until it matches or hv0.fw_check = 0. An HV board from before
# versioning reports 0.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
lcnc 0 0
run 0.3
version
lcnc 1 0
run 2
fault0.state
hv0.sim_fw_version = 0
run 0.1
fault0.state
fault0.fault
version
lcnc 0 0
run 0.1
lcnc 1 0
run 0.3
fault0.state
hv0.fw_check = 0
lcnc 0 0
run 0.1
lcnc 1 0
run 2
fault0.state
@match ^version fw=1 hv=1 hv_image=1 conf=0$
@match ^version fw=1 hv=0 hv_image=1 conf=0 hv_mismatch$
@expect fault0.state[1] == 1
@expect fault0.state[2] == 3
@expect fault0.fault[1] == 19
@expect fault0.state[3] == 3
@expect fault0.state[4] == 1
